/**
 * #10868 — the MLB web core checkpoint (`mlbGame.ts`): the team-paired headline,
 * the two-team history and All props, on a REAL retained final, through the web
 * owners the page already uses.
 *
 * FIXTURE — `mlbGame10868.fixtures.json`, generated by
 * `/tmp/cli-10868-mlbweb-gen/make_mlb_fixtures.py` and round-trip verified by
 * `/tmp/cli-10868-mlbweb-gen/verify_mlb_fixtures.py`: a mechanical extraction of
 * the CONSUMED fields only (its `_header` names every retained member, nested
 * rule and excluded member per source). Sources, sha256 checked before
 * extraction — White Sox at Astros 15321836, 2026-09-30, completed 3–7:
 *
 *   finalDetail   atlas-v6/raw/mlb-15321836-detail.json        (1221677b…)
 *   finalHistory  atlas-v6/raw/mlb-15321836-history.json       (0db9e147…)
 *   finalMarkets  atlas-v6/raw/mlb-15321836-game-markets.json  (42dfb489…), player_props[0:62]
 *
 * SECOND FIXTURE, FINAL ONLY — `mlbRunTotals10868.fixtures.json` (S1, read-only
 * here): the ENTIRE `game_question_matrix` member of that SAME game-markets body
 * (42dfb489…), which the reduced `finalMarkets` omits. The run-total tests join
 * it back onto `finalMarkets` (a CONSTRUCTED admission, named where used);
 * neither fixture is edited, and the matrix is never a before or live input
 * except where a test supplies it to prove it is refused.
 *
 * REAL proves the FINAL phase only. CONSTRUCTED here, and named where used:
 * every clock; the host's values (the hero pair through the page's own
 * `resolveProbability`, its accepted clock, `deliveryInterrupted`,
 * `liveClaimUnbacked`, the displayed score pair and `heroProjectedFinal`); the
 * before and live events (native BaseballRetainedAdapter10868Tests'
 * `beforeEdits` / `liveEdits`, key for key); and every one-key TEST MUTATION. A
 * constructed value is never real-game evidence. Jest runs in UTC; clock words
 * are compared through the screen's own formatter.
 */

